const path="/Users/jonvuri/Documents/Codex/2026-10-09/in-the-open-bitwig-project-the-4/outputs";
const doc=load("bassFinal").data.document;
const notes=load("notes");
const guide=`Rain Steps • Pocket Bass — timing reference

Project: Night Glass
Track: Bass — Undertow
Scene: 1
Loop: 32 quarter-note beats, 8 bars
Harmony: Dm9 / Bbmaj9 / Fmaj9 / C9, two bars each.
Existing sound: Sampler, left unchanged.

The companion Ghostnote snapshot contains the verified realized notes plus a nominal and groove overlay for each note. The nominal overlay records the authored rhythm on a sixteenth-note grid, including duration. The groove overlay records the authored signed offset from that nominal position. Positive is late; negative is early. Offsets were transferred from nearby Rain Steps kick and hi-hat onsets observed at 1/512 beat resolution. The drum's nominal grid is an interpretation, not a claim about its original author's intent.

Each claim depends only on its subject note's clip, onset, and duration; each groove claim also depends on its nominal claim. Ghostnote rereads or checks mark affected claims stale or remove claims whose event identity is no longer valid. Unchanged notes retain their claims. A moved note can receive a new event ID; do not treat its old claim as current or silently attach it to the new note. Read the live clip before further edits. The exported snapshot is a historical reference, not a live state check. Session base refs may expire.

Nominal onset | Realized onset | Offset (beats) | MIDI pitch | Duration
${notes.map(n=>`${n.nominal} | ${n.at} | ${n.offset} | ${n.pitch} | ${n.duration}`).join("\n")}
`;
text(await tools.apply_patch(`*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: ${path}/Pocket Bass.ghostnote\n${doc.split("\n").map(s=>"+"+s).join("\n")}\n*** Add File: ${path}/Pocket Bass timing reference.txt\n${guide.split("\n").map(s=>"+"+s).join("\n")}\n*** End Patch`));
text(await tools.mcp__ghostnote__show_launcher_clip_in_detail_editor({trackId:"17a0e91e-28b2-4ea1-ac91-89417b8faf2a",row:0}));
